     {
      "title": "Manager II, Internal Tools",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 7,
        "year": 2013
       },
       "endDate": {
        "month": 1,
        "year": 2016
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "2 yrs 7 mos",
      "description": "• Success with existing team resulted in management creating a new team specifically for automation of internal business processes and general tools development for me to lead.\n\n• Upon creation of the team, immediately engaged key business stakeholders to identify pain points and inefficient processes in client-facing teams.\n\n• New team consisted of combining two pre-existing teams with extremely disparate stacks: one .NET/Windows, the other Java/Linux. Had a successful release within three months of team creation while managing stakeholder expectations and coaching my team through learning a new framework.\n\n• Successfully adopted agile (scrum) methodologies to replace previous waterfall methodologies.\n\n• Currently working on automating installation of several company products, and a data warehouse to combine several disparate data sources into one view for better reporting.\n\n• Continued to contribute to development where appropriate, experimenting with node.js and AngularJS to better understand my team's needs. Also continued supporting extranet forms framework during crunch time so my team can focus on new systems instead of legacy ones.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Manager, Enterprise Applications",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 7,
        "year": 2012
       },
       "endDate": {
        "month": 7,
        "year": 2013
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "1 yr 1 mo",
      "description": "• Promoted to management after success in elevating development standards of the rest of the team. \n\n• Most of the year was taken up with migrating datacenters for over 10 individual applications from bare-metal machines to virtualized servers.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Senior Software Engineer",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 7,
        "year": 2008
       },
       "endDate": {
        "month": 7,
        "year": 2012
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "4 yrs 1 mo",
      "description": "• Led team in adopting best practices to evolve beyond cowboy coding. Introduced unit tests, bug tracking, proper monitoring, proper logging, migration of source control from VSS to Perforce, proper use of source control (branching, tagging releases), style standards, Resharper, automated builds, automated deployments, proper OO design techniques, introduction of MVC, dependency injection.\n\n• Single-handedly rewrote extranet forms framework from scratch in ASP.NET Web Forms and Windows Workflow Foundation, incorporating several best-practices improvements over the previous version (n-tier, automated builds, automated deployments, proper use of source control, relentless refactoring to eliminate code duplication). The forms initiate long-running workflows that automate integrations with several systems (CRM, automation platforms). Proved to be a success (30,000 forms after six years' production usage) - internal teams that rely on this framework re-organized around the concept of automation these forms allowed. Framework has allowed for massive improvements in work efficiency over the years - previously manual processes were now automated as much as possible. Proper design also greatly enhanced developer productivity through OO abstraction and automation of boilerplate code - creation of a new form now takes minutes instead of hours.\n\n• Created web front-end (Web Forms) for ticketing system that interacts with existing CRM ticketing system to simplify ticket entry for client internal teams. Ended up being successful enough to start to roll out to other teams for their use in managing their ticket queue.",
      "insights": ""
     }
